<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Physics on Craft &amp; Contemplation</title><link>https://wujipeng.com/tags/physics/</link><description>Recent content in Physics on Craft &amp; Contemplation</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 10:35:41 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://wujipeng.com/tags/physics/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>The Isomorphism Between Lenses and Encoders</title><link>https://wujipeng.com/writeups/lens_encoder/</link><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://wujipeng.com/writeups/lens_encoder/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="lens--encoder"&gt;Lens &lt;span class="katex"&gt;&lt;span class="katex-mathml"&gt;&lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"&gt;&lt;semantics&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;mo&gt;≅&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;annotation encoding="application/x-tex"&gt;\cong&lt;/annotation&gt;&lt;/semantics&gt;&lt;/math&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;span class="base"&gt;&lt;span class="strut" style="height:0.589em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mrel"&gt;≅&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; Encoder&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A camera lens and an image or audio encoder are isomorphic; both are fundamentally dimensionality-reduction functions that take high-dimensional physical reality as input: &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;span class="katex-display"&gt;&lt;span class="katex"&gt;&lt;span class="katex-mathml"&gt;&lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"&gt;&lt;semantics&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;mi&gt;f&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo&gt;:&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;msup&gt;&lt;mi mathvariant="double-struck"&gt;R&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;n&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/msup&gt;&lt;mo&gt;→&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;msup&gt;&lt;mi mathvariant="double-struck"&gt;R&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;d&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/msup&gt;&lt;mo separator="true"&gt;,&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mi&gt;d&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo&gt;≪&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mi&gt;n&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;annotation encoding="application/x-tex"&gt; f: \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}^d, d \ll n&lt;/annotation&gt;&lt;/semantics&gt;&lt;/math&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;span class="base"&gt;&lt;span class="strut" style="height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.10764em;"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mrel"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="base"&gt;&lt;span class="strut" style="height:0.7144em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mord"&gt;&lt;span class="mord mathbb"&gt;R&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="msupsub"&gt;&lt;span class="vlist-t"&gt;&lt;span class="vlist-r"&gt;&lt;span class="vlist" style="height:0.7144em;"&gt;&lt;span style="top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;"&gt;&lt;span class="pstrut" style="height:2.7em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"&gt;&lt;span class="mord mathnormal mtight"&gt;n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mrel"&gt;→&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="base"&gt;&lt;span class="strut" style="height:1.0935em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mord"&gt;&lt;span class="mord mathbb"&gt;R&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="msupsub"&gt;&lt;span class="vlist-t"&gt;&lt;span class="vlist-r"&gt;&lt;span class="vlist" style="height:0.8991em;"&gt;&lt;span style="top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;"&gt;&lt;span class="pstrut" style="height:2.7em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"&gt;&lt;span class="mord mathnormal mtight"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mpunct"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.1667em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mord mathnormal"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mrel"&gt;≪&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="base"&gt;&lt;span class="strut" style="height:0.4306em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mord mathnormal"&gt;n&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;p&gt;A lens compresses an infinite light field into a pixel matrix on the camera sensor:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt; 3D Scene
 ↓
 Lens
 ↓
2D Sensor Image&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;An encoder compresses some artificial sampling of infinite physical reality into a low-dimensional vector:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Order Emerges from Self-Assembly of Dissipative Structures</title><link>https://wujipeng.com/writeups/on-order/</link><pubDate>Tue, 28 Nov 2023 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://wujipeng.com/writeups/on-order/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Order emerges from the self-organization of dissipative structures, a phenomenon that is ubiquitous: Rayleigh-Bénard convection&lt;sup id="fnref:1"&gt;&lt;a href="#fn:1" class="footnote-ref" role="doc-noteref"&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; in fluid thermodynamics (regular cloud formations in the sky&lt;sup id="fnref:2"&gt;&lt;a href="#fn:2" class="footnote-ref" role="doc-noteref"&gt;2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;, solar granules&lt;sup id="fnref:3"&gt;&lt;a href="#fn:3" class="footnote-ref" role="doc-noteref"&gt;3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;, the hexagonal basalt columns of the Giant&amp;rsquo;s Causeway&lt;sup id="fnref:4"&gt;&lt;a href="#fn:4" class="footnote-ref" role="doc-noteref"&gt;4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;, mantle convection&lt;sup id="fnref:5"&gt;&lt;a href="#fn:5" class="footnote-ref" role="doc-noteref"&gt;5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;), the Belousov-Zhabotinsky reaction&lt;sup id="fnref:6"&gt;&lt;a href="#fn:6" class="footnote-ref" role="doc-noteref"&gt;6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; in chemical systems, and everything we know well — climate, cities, flames, explosions, stock markets, traffic, bee swarms, ecosystems, metabolism, life, consciousness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://wujipeng.com/img/stone.webp"
 alt="stone"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A dissipative structure is a steady-state system far from equilibrium that continuously exchanges matter and energy with its environment. Dissipative structures arise from input and dissipation: when energy or matter flows into a system, if there is a suitable mechanism to dissipate the excess energy, it can lead to a local increase in order or the formation of regularity. As dissipation continues, a complexity — or &amp;ldquo;intricacy&amp;rdquo; — that did not exist at first is born in the dissipative system: new behaviors, structures, and patterns arise on their own, organizing spontaneously, assembling automatically, running autonomously.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>